<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/empire-of-japan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empire%20of%20Japan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empire of Japan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After Hiroshima, Nagasaki and Soviet entry into the war, Japan surrenders aboard USS Missouri</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-states"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20States.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United States</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The United States emerges from the Second World War as a superpower</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-algeria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Algeria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Algeria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Sétif and Guelma massacres follow riots on 8 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/bailiwick-of-jersey"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bailiwick%20of%20Jersey.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bailiwick of Jersey</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jersey is liberated on 9 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/soviet-union"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Soviet%20Union.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Soviet Union</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Red Army captures Berlin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/nazi-germany"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazi%20Germany.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazi Germany</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hitler kills himself on 30 April; Germany surrenders unconditionally on 8 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/nguyen-dynasty"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nguyen%20dynasty.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nguyen dynasty</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Bao Dai abdicates to the Viet Minh on 30 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-indochina"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Indochina.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Indochina</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan overthrows French rule; Ho Chi Minh proclaims the Democratic Republic of Vietnam</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/indonesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indonesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indonesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sukarno and Mohammad Hatta proclaim independence on 17 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/shinto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Shinto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Shinto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Allied occupation’s Shinto Directive ends State Shinto</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/chavin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Chav%C3%ADn.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Chavín</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A debris flow buries much of the site and the modern town under mud</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/pan-africanism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Africanism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Africanism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Fifth Pan-African Congress in Manchester demands independence for Africa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-austria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Austria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Austria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 27 April Karl Renner, Adolf Schärf, Leopold Kunschak and Johann Koplenig declare Austria's secession from the Third Reich and set up a provisional government in Vienna, backed by Joseph Stalin.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/manchukuo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Manchukuo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Manchukuo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union declares war on 8 August and invades; Manchukuo units surrender or mutiny, Puyi abdicates on 17 August and is captured by the Soviets.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/socialist-federal-republic-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialist%20Federal%20Republic%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 29 November the Constituent Assembly abolishes the monarchy and proclaims the Federal People's Republic of Yugoslavia, a one-party state of six people's republics.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/malay"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Malay.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Malay</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Indonesia’s constitution makes Indonesian, developed from Riau Malay, the national language</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/maoism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Maoism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Maoism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Communist Party’s 7th national congress makes Mao Zedong Thought its unified ideology and writes it into the party constitution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/fascism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fascism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fascism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mussolini is executed by Italian partisans, Hitler commits suicide and the Nazi regime is dismantled</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-arabism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Arabism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Arabism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The League of Arab States is founded</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/independent-state-of-croatia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Independent%20State%20of%20Croatia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Independent State of Croatia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">NDH forces and civilians retreat to Austria; the British hand them to the Partisans, and the state falls after the Battle of Odžak on 25 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/ukrainian-ssr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ukrainian%20SSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ukrainian SSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Ukrainian SSR became a founding member of the United Nations, and Carpathian Ruthenia was transferred to it</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/democratic-republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Democratic%20Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Democratic Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After Japan's surrender the Việt Minh enter Hanoi in the August Revolution, and Hồ Chí Minh proclaims the Democratic Republic of Vietnam on 2 September</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/korea-under-japanese-rule"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Korea%20under%20Japanese%20rule.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Korea under Japanese rule</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan surrenders on 15 August, ending 35 years of colonial rule, and Korea is divided at the 38th parallel between American and Soviet forces</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/ho-chi-minh"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ho%20Chi%20Minh.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ho Chi Minh</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the August Revolution, reads the Declaration of Independence of the Democratic Republic of Vietnam</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/winston-churchill"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Winston%20Churchill.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Winston Churchill</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany surrenders; weeks later the Conservatives lose the general election to Labour</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-iwo-jima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Iwo%20Jima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Iwo Jima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Marines land on the south-eastern beaches, and by the evening 30,000 have come ashore</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-iwo-jima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Iwo%20Jima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Iwo Jima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A patrol raises the American flag on Mount Suribachi, and the second, larger flag is photographed by Joe Rosenthal</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-iwo-jima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Iwo%20Jima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Iwo Jima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Captain Samaji Inouye's 1,000 men charge the American lines, and the 3rd Marine Division reaches the northern coast</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-iwo-jima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Iwo%20Jima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Iwo Jima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The island is declared secure at 09:00 on 26 March after a final Japanese counterattack the night before</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-iwo-jima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Iwo%20Jima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Iwo Jima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The 147th Infantry Regiment spends three months clearing the Japanese who still hold out in caves and tunnels</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-okinawa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Okinawa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Okinawa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The US 77th Infantry Division takes the Kerama Islands west of Okinawa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-okinawa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Okinawa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Okinawa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Tenth Army lands on the Hagushi beaches and takes the Kadena and Yomitan airbases within hours</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-okinawa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Okinawa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Okinawa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">About 400 Japanese planes attack from Kyushu on 6 April, and the battleship Yamato sails on a suicide attack and is sunk</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-okinawa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Okinawa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Okinawa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Thirty-Second Army attacks across the whole front on three nights and is repulsed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-okinawa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Okinawa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Okinawa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The 96th Infantry Division takes Conical Hill, and the Marines fight for Sugar Loaf Hill</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-okinawa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Okinawa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Okinawa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Marines occupy Shuri Castle after the Japanese withdraw south</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-okinawa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Okinawa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Okinawa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">General Buckner is killed by Japanese artillery fire</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-okinawa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Okinawa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Okinawa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The last Japanese resistance ends and Ushijima and Chō die by suicide</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-bulge"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Bulge.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Bulge</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 16 January the U.S. First and Third Armies link up at Houffalize</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-bulge"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Bulge.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Bulge</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The offensive closes on 25 January, though the last German units do not return to their start line until February</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/berlin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Berlin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Berlin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Battle of Berlin ends with the city's capitulation and its division into four Allied sectors</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/hue"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hu%E1%BA%BF.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Huế</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Emperor Bảo Đại abdicates and the capital moves to Hanoi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/manila"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Manila.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Manila</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Battle of Manila destroys most of the city and civilians are killed in the Manila massacre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/buenos-aires"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Buenos%20Aires.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Buenos Aires</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The demonstration of 17 October at the Plaza de Mayo marks the emergence of Peronism</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/the-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/The%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>The Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Karl Popper's The Open Society and Its Enemies singles out Plato's state as a dystopia, and fragments of a different version are discovered at Nag Hammadi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/dresden-codex"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dresden%20Codex.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dresden Codex</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The codex is kept in a flooded basement during the bombing of Dresden and suffers serious water damage</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/himeji-castle"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Himeji%20Castle.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Himeji Castle</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Himeji was heavily bombed, and the castle survived intact</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/sukarno"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sukarno.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sukarno</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sukarno and Hatta proclaim Indonesian independence on 17 August, and the next day Sukarno is elected president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/quit-india-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Quit%20India%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Quit India movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">All jailed nationalists are released after the Labour Party wins the British election</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/nazism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nazi Germany collapses, and the full extent of the Holocaust is disclosed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/populism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Populism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Populism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The mass mobilisation of 17 October in Argentina, often considered the founding moment of Peronism</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/gnosticism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Gnosticism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Gnosticism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Nag Hammadi library is found near Nag Hammadi in Upper Egypt</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/tenrikyo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tenrikyo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tenrikyo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The period of Tenrikyo's designation as one of the groups of Sect Shinto, which began in 1908, ends</span></li></ul></section>
